{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-358",
  "title": "MotionsSpec | Web Essentials",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "MotionsSpec | Web Essentials"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Positioning MotionSpec as part of a **retainer package** makes sense, especially under your *Web Essentials* tier. Here’s why:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Why Web Essentials Fits"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Deliverable alignment**: MotionSpec work is about capturing, replicating, and standardizing motion/scroll interactions. That ties directly to *“crafting streamlined, engaging, highly-interactive web experiences”*—the exact language in the Web Essentials plan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Recurring value**: Each new client/story can be onboarded into the same MotionSpec workflow. That creates predictable recurring work (schema evolution, new adapter integrations, performance checks)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Support & maintenance**: MotionSpec tooling needs runtime testing, bug fixes when libraries update (GSAP, Framer Motion, etc.), and improvements to capture quality. This sits well under *“monthly site maintenance”* and *“technical support & training.”*"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "How You Could Frame It"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**For MVP**: Deliver it as an internal tool (Storytime MVP with hand-authored animations)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-12",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**For Retainer Pitch**: Position MotionSpec as the *“next step”*—turning what’s now manual into a repeatable system."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- *“We can automatically capture and standardize complex animations from live sites, then replay or repurpose them across stories. This makes the process faster for us, but also ensures clients get higher-fidelity interactive storytelling without added cost.”*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-15",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**DX + UX win**: Clients don’t need to understand the tech, but they feel the benefits: faster iteration, more consistent experiences, and the ability to push updates without full rebuilds."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Timing & Sales Angle"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-19",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Don’t pitch until after MVP** — you’re right. MotionSpec is easier to sell once they *see Storytime live*."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-20",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Pitch as an upgrade path** — Web Essentials subscribers “lock in” early access to MotionSpec workflows as part of their monthly retainer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-21",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Future flexibility** — if MotionSpec matures into a standalone tool, you could graduate it into the *Full-Service* tier or spin it into its own licensing model."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}